BraleModuleIntegration
├── when a keeper calls executeAction
│   ├── it should return true
│   ├── it should emit ActionExecuted and RedemptionInitiated
│   ├── it should credit the deposit address with the amount
│   ├── it should leave the rails allowance to the module at zero
│   └── it should leave the module balance at zero
├── when executeAction is called repeatedly
│   └── it should use nonces 0, 1, 2 with unique ids
├── when the token charges a recipient fee
│   ├── it should return false with ActionFailed "Module execution reverted"
│   └── it should leave balances and nonce unchanged
├── when the token charges a sender fee
│   └── it should return false with ActionFailed "Module execution reverted"
├── when the deposit address is the PaymentRails
│   └── it should emit ActionFailed "Deposit address is PaymentRails"
├── when previewExecution is called
│   └── it should return the 1:1 estimate and the output token
├── when the rails owner reconfigures the deposit address
│   └── it should send the next redemption to the new address
├── when an EOA calls module.execute directly
│   └── it should revert with BraleModule_NotPaymentRails
└── when two borrowers each have their own rails and module
    ├── it should credit only each borrower's own deposit address
    └── it should produce different ids for the same nonce
